Subject: [PATCH] Tools: Dump Process Memory (Build 135)

Some games only put together their NEX settings (game-server ID and
access key) while they run, so the key can't be read from the .code
dump. Governor of Poker is one: its engine reads game_id/access_key from
a settings list filled in at run time, and neither value is in its code
or RomFS.

Tools > Dump Process Memory (enabled while a game runs) writes every
readable memory region of each running game (title IDs 00040000xxxxxxxx;
not system modules or applets) to
<user>/dump/memory/<title id>-<date-time>.bin, with a .txt list of the
regions (address, size, offset in the file, state, permissions). It
reads under the HLE lock, so it can be used while the game runs. Dump
after the game has tried to go online. Nothing leaves the machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
